# Wind-driven dust emission: the three boundary fields, the gathers, and Kok
# (2014) equation 18 in the source term. DUST-3 item 4.
#
# WHAT THIS IS FOR. ExoPlaSim's own dust source is one line,
# `mmr(:,:,NLEV,ic) = fcoeff*land`, which emits as much from forest as from salt
# pan and SETS a concentration rather than adding a flux. `notes/dust.md`
# reopened the in-model question at a land-mean optical depth of 0.10 and this
# world crosses it by 3.8x, so a prescribed field is no longer defensible: the
# dust changes the winds and the winds change the dust. This is the piece that
# closes that loop, and `aeolian/notes/in-model-dust.md` calls it the largest
# mechanical one.
#
# SUPERSEDED IN ONE PLACE, and the subtree is what is right. The quadrature
# below spaces its nodes evenly in probability over [0, 1] and scales the total
# by 1/dustnq. `dustsrc` in the subtree spaces them evenly in SURVIVAL over
# [0, S_t] and scales by S_t/dustnq, because the probability-space rule's
# highest node is a ceiling that does not move with the threshold and returns
# exactly zero wherever u*t clears it. world-494 replaced the same rule offline;
# world-2lsg replaced it here. Read the subtree for the quadrature and this file
# for everything else.
#
# THE STANDING DECISION IT IMPLEMENTS. The per-cell source map stays OUTSIDE the
# model. Which ground can emit is a question about lithology, the lake solution
# and the soil, and answering it needs the mesh export that the climate model has
# never seen. So the model reads prepared surface fields and does not recompute
# soil erodibility itself, exactly as it does for albedo, roughness and
# soil-water capacity. What it computes is everything that responds to the
# weather.
#
# DEFAULTS OFF. `ldustemit = 0` keeps the legacy source line untouched, gathers
# nothing extra, reads no surface field and makes no extra collective call, so
# one executable runs both arms of an A/B and the arms differ only by a namelist
# key. That is `WORKFLOW.md` A3 and it is load-bearing: the low-I/O patch changes
# the restart layout, so arms built either side of a rebuild cannot share a
# restart at all.
#
# BASE. ExoPlaSim 3.4.2 plus the resident stack, plus
# exoplasim-3.4.2-aerocore-defects.patch and
# exoplasim-3.4.2-aerosol-deposition.patch, which have to be applied first and in
# that order. That base is
#
#   aerocore.f90  045b566657233ead40cfc4e8d9cf97c82c8bb8253f9ea187afadbc6967f74485
#   aeromod.f90   aebf8dedb5dc84fc134cc7836636512be879e6b21a8d893a666bb31fc90f1856
#   surfmod.f90   1c0c8d8aeb2b9f24704e6a4c212e0a9b51c5555d3b6913632e690dae470d08ca
#   plasim.f90    ebc5bc8352e5433ac2ed5275868ea906aa930ee6b196b3586676f789b8881b4f
#   make_plasim   edd995a052c89d43121840e6ed5bc321cf9bfddd4a3180c927daa0b6998bc367
#
# surfmod.f90 already carries exoplasim-3.4.2-prescribed-dust.patch and
# plasim.f90 and make_plasim already carry the denergy-accumulator and
# lowio-first-record patches, so those shas are the composed resident result and
# not pristine 3.4.2. NOTHING HERE TOUCHES radmod.f90.
#
# RESIDENT-DESTINED, NOT YET RESIDENT. Listed in `PENDING_PATCHES` in
# `exoplasim/scripts/rebuild_binaries.py`; it moves to `RESIDENT_PATCHES` in the
# commit that applies it and rebuilds every binary.
#
# WHAT IT ADDS.
#
#  1. THREE SURFACE BOUNDARY FIELDS, codes 1801, 1802 and 1803, registered in
#     `surface_ini` beside the rest. Three and no fewer, and the split is decided
#     by where each quantity enters the flux rather than by tidiness.
#
#       1801  dsrcw   erodible fraction x clipped clay fraction. Both are LINEAR
#                     prefactors on the flux, so their product is sufficient and
#                     a second field would be redundant.
#       1802  ddrage  the Marticorena-Bergametti (1995) drag partition of the
#                     erodible bed. Separate because it scales u* itself, so it
#                     sits inside the threshold comparison AND inside the
#                     fragmentation exponent and does not commute out to a
#                     prefactor. Folding it into 1801 would be wrong.
#       1803  dwpr    the Fecan et al. (1999) residual moisture w', percent.
#                     Separate because the moisture gate also needs the model's
#                     own soil water, which is already in memory.
#
#     All three are dimensionless-or-percent pure functions of terrain,
#     lithology, the lake solution and the soil, written by
#     `aeolian/scripts/build_dust_source_fields.py`. Everything time-varying --
#     wind, soil water, snow -- comes from the model.
#
#  2. `aero_surf`, a new subroutine called from `plasim.f90` by EVERY rank. It
#     cannot live in `aero_ini`: that runs inside an `if (mypid == NROOT)` block
#     and `mpsurfgp` is collective, so a rank that never enters it hangs. It
#     reads the three fields, gathers them ONCE into the global arrays `aerocore`
#     works on, and aborts loudly if 1801 is absent or zero -- surfmod skips a
#     missing surface file in silence, so the alternative is a run that emits
#     nothing and says nothing.
#
#  3. TWO PER-STEP GATHERS in `aero_main`, `dsnow` and `dwatc`, made only when
#     `ldustemit = 1`. Nothing else is needed: the wind is `zu` and `zv`, which
#     `prepare_uvps` has already gathered AND flipped, and air density and
#     temperature are `rhog` and `temp` inside `aerocore`. The design note
#     expected three more gathers, of friction velocity, soil wetness and snow;
#     the friction velocity one is unnecessary because the scheme must NOT use
#     the model's grid-cell stress -- see point 5.
#
#     EVERY GATHERED FIELD IS FLIPPED IN LATITUDE, `f(:,NLAT+1-j) = zgath(:,j)`,
#     which is the convention `plasim.f90` sets with
#     `daeros(:,NLAT+1-jlat,:,1) = zmmr(:,jlat,:)` and the one the defect patch
#     fixed the land mask and the solar zenith angle to. It is written the same
#     way round on purpose and was checked against both, because getting it
#     backwards is silent: it drives the emission in the mirror hemisphere and
#     this world's land is not hemispherically symmetric.
#
#  4. THIRTEEN CALIBRATION KEYS IN `aero_nl`, none with a Fortran default, all of
#     them owned by `aeolian/config/dust.yaml` and written into the namelist by
#     `run_exoplasim.py` from the provenance file beside the fields.
#     `aero_ini` ABORTS on `ldustemit = 1` with any of them unset, the way it
#     already does for `vdaero` and the way `radini` does for `dustqlw`. A
#     plausible-looking default here would be a fourth place for a constant one
#     file already owns; a silently zeroed threshold would emit from the whole
#     planet at every wind.
#
#     The two thresholds arrive ALREADY SCALED for this planet's gravity, by the
#     fourth root of the gravity ratio and not the square root. The scaling is
#     applied outside because that is where `config/planet.yaml` lives, and both
#     thresholds take the same factor, which leaves (u*st - u*st0)/u*st0
#     unchanged, so Cd and alpha are invariant under it.
#
#  5. KOK (2014) EQUATIONS 18a AND 18b in `dustsrc`, read from the paper rather
#     than from a summary of it, evaluated over a Weibull distribution of subgrid
#     wind and ADDED as a flux: d(mmr) = F g dt / dp. Not the White or Kawamura
#     saltation flux, which is the HORIZONTAL flux in kg/m/s and needs a
#     sandblasting efficiency before it is a dust emission.
#
#     The friction velocity is built from the model's BOTTOM-LEVEL WIND through
#     the AEOLIAN roughness of the erodible patch, not from the model's own
#     surface stress. That is a declared position of this project, argued in
#     `aeolian/config/dust.yaml`: MB95 partitions stress between a bed and
#     centimetre-scale roughness ELEMENTS standing on it, and a 15 km orographic
#     variance is not a roughness element. Driving the partition with the
#     grid-cell roughness returns zero emission over 99% of the erodible area,
#     which is a category error rather than a result. Its cost is stated rather
#     than hidden: sheltering of an erodible patch by the terrain around it is
#     not represented, and that biases emission high.
#
#  6. One inherited build defect. `aerocore.f90` has used `aeromod` since the
#     deposition patch and `make_plasim` never said so, which a parallel make can
#     lose. The dependency line is corrected here.
#
# WHAT IT DELIBERATELY IS NOT. No size bins: DUST-8 decided single mode and says
# what that costs. No longwave aerosol term and no `apart` fix: both live in
# `radmod.f90`, which another branch is editing, and they are item 5 and upstream
# defect 1. No change to transport, settling or removal.
#
# PREDICTIONS, STATED BEFORE THEY RUN, per `WORKFLOW.md` A3. The comparator is
# `aeolian/analysis/dust_baseline.json`, whose central-roughness total emission
# was computed offline from the SAME climatology, the SAME map and the SAME
# `dust.yaml`. Take the number from that file rather than from here.
#
#  a. EXACT AGREEMENT IS NOT EXPECTED AND IT WOULD BE SUSPICIOUS. The offline
#     chain fits a Weibull to 1,463 three-hourly samples and applies it around a
#     12-bin climatological MEAN wind; the model applies the same Weibull around
#     its own INSTANTANEOUS wind, so at `dustwk` = the measured shape the
#     sub-daily variance is counted twice. The flux is convex in u* above
#     threshold, so Jensen's inequality fixes the SIGN and it is not a guess:
#     the in-model total must EXCEED the offline central total. Predicted 3x to
#     10x, the upper end being the 8.8x the offline chain itself measured when
#     the wind tail went from synoptic to sub-daily.
#     FALSIFIED BY an in-model total BELOW the offline one, which cannot happen
#     for a correct implementation of a convex flux and would mean the emission
#     is not reaching the cells the field marks -- check the latitude flip first.
#
#  b. THE SHARP COMPARISON IS THE NEAR-DELTA ARM. Set `dustwk` to 50 and the
#     quadrature collapses onto the gridbox mean, so the model's own resolved
#     variability replaces the fitted Weibull -- which is what that Weibull was
#     standing in for, since it was fitted to this model's own winds. That total
#     must land within a factor of 5 of the offline central figure, either side.
#     FALSIFIED BY a factor beyond 10, which is structural rather than
#     distributional: units, the mixing-ratio conversion, or the threshold.
#
#  c. LINEARITY IN 1801, an exact identity and the strongest test here. Doubling
#     field 1801 must double the total emission to round-off, because erodible
#     fraction and clay fraction are linear prefactors -- which is the entire
#     argument for packing them into one field. FALSIFIED BY any ratio other
#     than 2.
#
#  d. TIMESTEP INDEPENDENCE. Halve `deltsec` and emission per unit time must not
#     move by more than round-off: the Kok flux contains no timestep and the
#     mixing-ratio conversion's `deltsec` cancels against twice as many steps.
#     FALSIFIED BY a rate that scales with the step, which would mean `deltsec`
#     is applied twice or the flux is being read as a concentration.
#
#  e. THE HEMISPHERE. Annual-mean bottom-level dust must correlate with field
#     1801 more strongly than with its north-south mirror. This world's land is
#     not hemispherically symmetric, so it can fail, and it is the direct test
#     of point 3.
#
#  f. THE GRAVITY TERM. Feeding the UNSCALED Earth thresholds must RAISE
#     emission, by about 30% at the central roughness, which is what the offline
#     chain measured when the term went in. FALSIFIED BY the opposite sign or by
#     more than a factor of two.
#
# Two known sources of small disagreement, stated so they are not rediscovered as
# defects: the offline chain uses dry-air R = 287.05 J/kg/K for air density while
# the model uses its own declared `gascon`, and the offline reference height is
# built from surface air temperature while the model uses its bottom-level
# temperature. Both are a few percent on u* and neither approaches the brackets
# above.
#
# VERIFIED WITHOUT COMPILING THE MODEL. Applied to a scratch mirror of the base
# above, checked with `gfortran -fsyntax-only -O3 -cpp -ffixed-line-length-132`
# at both 4-byte and 8-byte default reals against the real module files, and
# reversed cleanly newest-first the way `resident_ok()` unwinds the stack.
